        "raw": "<p>I was playing a game in iOS against Grand Warlord Voss involving Haka in the Temple of Zhu Long. &nbsp;Haka had Savage Mana in play, and there were two interactions that seemed to be at odds:</p><p>1. &nbsp;The Temple had Resurrection Ritual in play. &nbsp;Resurrection Ritual says that whenever a villain target is destroyed, put it under Resurrection Ritual. &nbsp;This would seem to contradict Savage Mana, because Savage Mana says to put a target that Haka destroys under Savage Mana. &nbsp;When Haka killed one of Voss&#39; minions, the game gave the option of putting the minion under Savage Mana or under Resurrection Ritual.</p><p>2. &nbsp;When Haka tried to kill a Shinobi Assassin, however, the game would not give the option of putting the Shinobi Assassin under Savage Mana; it wouldn&#39;t let Savage Mana take effect.</p><p>Is this as intended? &nbsp;Should Resurrection Ritual trump Savage Mana (or whichever is played first should take effect first)? &nbsp;Should Haka be permitted to put Shinobi Assassins under Savage Mana?</p><p>&nbsp;</p>",
