        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/matchstickman/{size}/1880_2.png",
        "created_at": "2017-05-15T21:29:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>These are not at odds.</p><p>Shinobi Assassin has different wording to both Savage Mana and Resurrection Ritual, the key being</p><p><span>\"When this card <em><strong>would be </strong></em>destroyed, move it to the top of a Hero deck instead.\"</span></p><p>the Assassin is never actually destroyed, it is instead moved.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Both Savage Mana and Resurrection Ritual rely on the target being destroyed so trigger at the same time, thus the players get to choose what happens to the villain target.</p>",
